From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the Lenovo 10w

Add the Lenovo 10w (82ST, 82SU), a 10.1" Snapdragon 7c Gen 2 tablet with
a pogo-pin keyboard. No tree existed for it. Its DSDT
(aarch64-laptops/build misc/lenovo-l10w) carries Qualcomm's reference
subsystem ID QSIP7180, as the Acer Aspire 1's and the LIVA QC710's do,
and its firmware images are signed by Qualcomm's production root like
Qualcomm's reference ones. So the SoC side, the reserved memory and the
regulator table are the Aspire 1's, and the board values are the ones
the 10w's DSDT gives.

The DSDT's I2C1, I2C8 and IC10 sit at 0x880000, 0xa84000 and 0xa8c000,
which are i2c0, i2c7 and i2c9. GpioInt pins below 0xc0 are TLMM GPIOs.

- The touchscreen and pen (TSC1, Wacom WACF2200) are at 0x0a on i2c0
  at 1 MHz, with the HID descriptor at 0x01 and the interrupt on GPIO 9,
  level low with a pull-up. Its PEP entry raises GPIO 4, waits 10 ms,
  releases the reset on GPIO 8 and waits 100 ms, which the tree models
  as a switched supply and an active-low reset.
- A HID device (GSEN, QTEC0001) is at 0x05 on i2c7 with its descriptor
  at 0x20 and its interrupt on GPIO 33, level low with a pull-up. Lenovo
  lists an accelerometer and a gyroscope, and the device's name points
  to them, but the tables don't say what it reports.
- The power key and volume down are the PMIC's power-on keys (BTNS on
  PM01 pins 0 and 1, usages 0x81 and 0xea), so pon stays on and resin
  reports KEY_VOLUMEDOWN.
- Storage is eMMC, as Lenovo's specification says. SDC1 takes LDO19_A
  at 2.96 V and LDO12_A at 1.8 V, as on the Aspire 1.
- USB takes LDO11_A, LDO17_A, LDO3_C and LDO4_A, Bluetooth takes LDO1_C,
  LDO2_C and LDO10_C with its UART wake on GPIO 41, and Wi-Fi's COEX
  entry votes LDO9_A, all as on the Aspire 1. The Aspire's USB PHY
  tuning values are its own board's, so they are left at the defaults.
- The PEP configures the I2C pins with the internal pull-up at 2 mA.
- The images' load addresses fit the Aspire 1's reserved memory, with
  the ADSP at 0x2800000 and the Wi-Fi-only modem at 0x2000000.

These are left out, for lack of a driver or of evidence.

- The display. The panel is a 1200x1920 MIPI DSI panel, a B101UAN08
  or an NV101WUM by the panel ID GPU0._ROM selects on. The B101UAN08's
  timings and size are those of the kernel's auo,b101uan08.3, but its
  init sequence writes the gate registers in the opposite order, and no
  driver knows the NV101WUM. So MDSS stays off and the screen stays on
  the firmware's framebuffer. The GPU is enabled but binds only with
  msm.separate_gpu_kms=1.
- Audio. The ALC5682 codec is at 0x1a on i2c9 with its interrupt on
  GPIO 11 and its supply switch on GPIO 83, but the speaker amplifier
  and its I2S port aren't in the tables.
- Volume up (BTNS PM01 pin 0x209), the tablet-mode indicator (CIND,
  ID9001, PNP0C60, on GPIO 43), USB-C orientation and DisplayPort
  (UCS0 on GPIO 32), the cameras and the battery, which the PMIC's
  fuel gauge reports and Linux has no driver for on this PMIC.
- The reserved GPIOs 58 to 62 stay as on the Aspire 1. The 10w's audio
  device uses GPIO 58, so that one isn't protected, but nothing here
  needs the range.

The firmware is in Lenovo's driver packages for the 82ST and 82SU and
goes in qcom/sc7180/LENOVO/82ST. Not booted on the tablet yet.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-lenovo-10w.dts | 524 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 524 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-lenovo-10w.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-lenovo-10w.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-lenovo-10w.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b62310d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-lenovo-10w.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,524 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * Lenovo 10w (82ST, 82SU)
+ *
+ * Snapdragon 7c Gen 2 tablet with a pogo-pin keyboard. Its DSDT carries
+ * Qualcomm's reference subsystem ID (QSIP7180), like the Acer Aspire 1's,
+ * so the SoC side follows the Aspire 1 tree. The board values are the
+ * ones the 10w's DSDT gives: the Wacom touchscreen on i2c0, a HID device
+ * on i2c7, eMMC storage and the power and volume-down keys on the PMIC.
+ * The 1200x1920 MIPI DSI panel has no driver yet, so the display stays
+ * on the firmware's framebuffer.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
+
+#include "sc7180.dtsi"
+
+#include "pm6150.dtsi"
+#include "pm6150l.dtsi"
+
+/delete-node/ &tz_mem;
+/delete-node/ &ipa_fw_mem;
+
+/ {
+	model = "Lenovo 10w";
+	compatible = "lenovo,10w", "qcom,sc7180";
+	chassis-type = "tablet";
+
+	aliases {
+		bluetooth0 = &bluetooth;
+		hsuart0 = &uart3;
+		wifi0 = &wifi;
+	};
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		gpu_mem: zap-shader@80840000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x80840000 0 0x2000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		venus_mem: venus@85b00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x85b00000 0 0x500000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		mpss_mem: mpss@86000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x86000000 0x0 0x2000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		adsp_mem: adsp@8e400000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x8e400000 0x0 0x2800000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		wlan_mem: wlan@93900000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x93900000 0x0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
+	vdd_touchscreen: touchscreen-regulator {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vdd_touchscreen";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&ts_pwr_en_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&gpu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&gpu_zap_shader {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/LENOVO/82ST/qcdxkmsuc7180.mbn";
+};
+
+&i2c0 {
+	clock-frequency = <1000000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	touchscreen@a {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0xa>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x1>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		vdd-supply = <&vdd_touchscreen>;
+		post-power-on-delay-ms = <10>;
+
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 8 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		post-reset-deassert-delay-ms = <100>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&ts_int_default>, <&ts_reset_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c7 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	hid@5 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x5>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x20>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 33 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&gsen_int_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&pm6150_resin {
+	linux,code = <KEY_VOLUMEDOWN>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	memory-region = <&adsp_mem>;
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/LENOVO/82ST/qcadsp7180.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_mpss {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/LENOVO/82ST/qcmpss7180_nm.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&sdhc_1 {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&sdc1_default>;
+	pinctrl-1 = <&sdc1_sleep>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+	vmmc-supply = <&vreg_l19a_2p9>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&vreg_l12a_1p8>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&uart3 {
+	/delete-property/interrupts;
+	interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 604 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			      <&tlmm 41 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+
+	pinctrl-1 = <&qup_uart3_sleep>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	bluetooth: bluetooth {
+		compatible = "qcom,wcn3991-bt";
+		vddio-supply = <&vreg_l10a_1p8>;
+		vddxo-supply = <&vreg_l1c_1p8>;
+		vddrf-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p3>;
+		vddch0-supply = <&vreg_l10c_3p3>;
+		max-speed = <3200000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&usb_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_1_dwc3 {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+};
+
+&usb_1_hsphy {
+	vdd-supply = <&vreg_l4a_0p8>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l11a_1p8>;
+	vdda-phy-dpdm-supply = <&vreg_l17a_3p0>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_1_qmpphy {
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l4a_0p8>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l3c_1p2>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&venus {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/LENOVO/82ST/qcvss7180.mbn";
+};
+
+&wifi {
+	vdd-0.8-cx-mx-supply = <&vreg_l9a_0p6>;
+	vdd-1.8-xo-supply = <&vreg_l1c_1p8>;
+	vdd-1.3-rfa-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p3>;
+	vdd-3.3-ch0-supply = <&vreg_l10c_3p3>;
+	vdd-3.3-ch1-supply = <&vreg_l11c_3p3>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&apps_rsc {
+	regulators-0 {
+		compatible = "qcom,pm6150-rpmh-regulators";
+		qcom,pmic-id = "a";
+
+		vreg_s1a_1p1: smps1 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1128000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1128000>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l4a_0p8: ldo4 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <824000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <928000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l9a_0p6: ldo9 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <488000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l10a_1p8: ldo10 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l11a_1p8: ldo11 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l12a_1p8: ldo12 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l13a_1p8: ldo13 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l14a_1p8: ldo14 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l15a_1p8: ldo15 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l16a_2p7: ldo16 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2496000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3304000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l17a_3p0: ldo17 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2920000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3232000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l18a_2p8: ldo18 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2496000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3304000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l19a_2p9: ldo19 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2960000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <2960000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	regulators-1 {
+		compatible = "qcom,pm6150l-rpmh-regulators";
+		qcom,pmic-id = "c";
+
+		vreg_s8c_1p3: smps8 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1120000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1408000>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l1c_1p8: ldo1 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1616000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1984000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l2c_1p3: ldo2 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1168000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l3c_1p2: ldo3 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1144000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l4c_1p8: ldo4 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1648000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3304000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l5c_1p8: ldo5 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1648000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3304000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l6c_2p9: ldo6 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <2950000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l7c_3p0: ldo7 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3312000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l8c_1p8: ldo8 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l9c_2p9: ldo9 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2952000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <2952000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l10c_3p3: ldo10 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3400000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l11c_3p3: ldo11 {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
